Z||000004||Dingo||04-02-2001||06:10 PM||||Dude,<P>Sorry to hear about your misfortune with this person. I hate to say it but it happens. I had it happen to me twice. Lucky it was not for that much money but I did not get anything back from either expereince except some newly aquired knowledge not to trust anyone with my car. Did you check the guy out and ask for references before having him do any of the work? Ask for photos of before and after conversions. Ask for peoples names and their phone numbers and to see their cars before having a conversion done. I belong to another club too and I have seen the same things happen to them. You can alays take the guy to small claims court and try to get your money back even though he did the work you might get a 100% refund on the conversion. Also let other club members know this guys name so we dont get hosed over by this guy. Takes a long time to build a good rep... takes only a few minutes to screw it up.<BR>Also if you can contact others that have the same problems you might be able to go in together when it comes time to sue this bonehead.<P>goodluck||||reg||11
